description: Review, test, branch, and commit after implementation; never push to production
alwaysApply: true
---

# After implementation

1. Review the diff yourself. Look for regressions in related handlers, DB functions, and callers.
2. Run the full test suite (`go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `golangci-lint run` in `backend-go`) and fix failures.
3. Show exactly what changed: files, behavior, and test results.
4. Do not push to production or to the default branch.
5. Put the work on a new branch and commit it. Push only when asked.

```
git checkout -b <short-topic-branch>
git add <relevant files>
git commit -m "<why the change was made>"
```
